From: RG35XX Java Platform
Task: RGJ-RC1-011CH
Subject: [PATCH] RG35XX: force opaque bitmap glyphs and default native audio on

Device evidence from RC1-011CG shows two independent presentation problems:
1) the bitmap text path reaches drawRGB(processAlpha=true), but PlatformGraphics
   getColor() is a 24-bit RGB value. RG35XXBitmapText copied that value verbatim,
   leaving alpha=0, so every glyph pixel was fully transparent;
2) native media now advances correctly to END_OF_MEDIA, but the libretro pump
   submits AudioBatch only when soundEnabled is true. The upstream global is
   zero-initialized and only changes when a frontend exposes freej2me_sound.
   Minimal RG35XX frontends may not expose that variable, silently discarding
   otherwise valid PCM while completion events still PASS.

Keep explicit frontend `freej2me_sound=off` authoritative, but make the runtime
fallback default `on`. Normalize bitmap glyph colors to opaque ARGB before they
enter drawRGB.

--- a/src/org/recompile/mobile/RG35XXBitmapText.java
+++ b/src/org/recompile/mobile/RG35XXBitmapText.java
@@ -32,11 +32,14 @@ public final class RG35XXBitmapText
     public static int[] render(String text, int argb)
     {
         final int bitmapWidth = width(text);
+        /* PlatformGraphics.getColor() returns RGB (0xRRGGBB). drawRGB with
+         * processAlpha=true interprets a missing high byte as alpha=0, which
+         * made every RG35XX fallback glyph fully transparent on device. */
+        final int opaqueArgb = argb | 0xFF000000;
         if(bitmapWidth <= 0) return new int[0];
         if(bitmapWidth > Integer.MAX_VALUE / CELL_HEIGHT) return new int[0];
 
         final int[] pixels = new int[bitmapWidth * CELL_HEIGHT];
         for(int i = 0; i < text.length(); i++)
         {
-            drawGlyph8x12(pixels, bitmapWidth, text.charAt(i), i * CELL_WIDTH, argb);
+            drawGlyph8x12(pixels, bitmapWidth, text.charAt(i), i * CELL_WIDTH, opaqueArgb);
         }
         return pixels;
     }
--- a/src/libretro/freej2me_libretro.c
+++ b/src/libretro/freej2me_libretro.c
@@ -158,7 +158,9 @@ int rotateScreen = 0; /* Allows rotations between 0, 90, 180 and 270 degrees */
 int phoneType = 0; /* 0=Standard (Nokia/Sony/Samsung), 1=LG, 2=Motorola/SoftBank, 3=Motorola Triplets... */
 int backlightColor = 1; /* 0=Disabled, 1=Green, etc. */
 int gameFPS = 60; /* Auto(0), 60, 55, 50, 45, 40, 35, 30, 25, 20, 15, 10 */
-int soundEnabled; /* also acts as a boolean */
+/* RG35XX frontends may not expose freej2me_sound at all. Default on, while
+ * check_variables() still honors an explicit frontend value of "off". */
+int soundEnabled = 1; /* also acts as a boolean */
 int customMidi; /* Also acts as a boolean */
 int customFont; /* Also acts as a boolean */
 int fontOffset = 0; /* -4, -3, -2, -1, 0 (Default), 1, 2, 3, 4 */
